{"header":"<h1>Module type <code><span>Pqueue.OrderedType</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"melange","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Stdlib","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Pqueue","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"OrderedType","href":"#","kind":"module-type"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Input signature of the functors <a href=\"../MakeMin/index.html\"><code>MakeMin</code></a> and <a href=\"../MakeMax/index.html\"><code>MakeMax</code></a>.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span>;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The type of elements.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-compare\"><a href=\"#val-compare\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">let</span> compare: <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span> int;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>A total ordering function to compare elements.</p><p>This is a two-argument function <code>f</code> such that <code>f e1 e2</code> is zero if the elements <code>e1</code> and <code>e2</code> are equal, <code>f e1 e2</code> is strictly negative if <code>e1</code> is smaller than <code>e2</code>, and <code>f e1 e2</code> is strictly positive if <code>e1</code> is greater than <code>e2</code>.</p><p>The generic structural comparison function <a href=\"../../index.html#val-compare\"><code>Stdlib.compare</code></a> is a suitable ordering function for element types such as <code>int</code> or <code>string</code>.</p></div></div>"}